# Project rules for AI agents (screeps_ai)

## Git governance
- **NEVER run git-mutating commands**: no `commit`, `push`, `tag`, `merge`, `rebase`, `reset --hard`, `checkout --`, `branch -d`, etc. Read-only git is allowed: `status`, `diff`, `log`, `rev-parse`, `show`.
- **The human performs every commit.** A pre-commit hook enforces this mechanically — never attempt to bypass it (no `--no-verify`, no `ALLOW_COMMIT` manipulation, no hook editing).
- When a workflow needs a commit reference (e.g. `baseline_commit`), use read-only `git rev-parse HEAD`.

## Code
- Follow `_bmad-output/planning-artifacts/architecture/architecture-screeps_ai-2026-08-07/ARCHITECTURE-SPINE.md` — AD-1..AD-10 are binding.
- All MVP constants live in `src/config.ts`; never hardcode tunables.

## Model routing
- **dev-story / dev-auto** → run on the Cline `bm-dev` profile (cheap/free model).
- **code-review / tea** (bmad-tea, bmad-testarch-*) → run on the Cline `bm-review` profile (smart model).
- Before invoking code-review or any bmad-tea / bmad-testarch-* skill, confirm the `bm-review` profile is active; if `bm-dev` is active, ask Fliko to switch before proceeding.
- After dev-story / dev-auto completes, remind Fliko to switch to `bm-review` before running code-review or tea.
- Record the model used in each story's Dev Agent Record ("Agent Model Used") for audit.
